statement:
Fix a natural number $n$, and let $r, s$ be natural numbers with $r \le n$ and $s \le n$. Then the binary Krawtchouk polynomials satisfy
\[
  \sum_{x=0}^{n} \binom{n}{x}\, K_r^{(n)}(x)\, K_s^{(n)}(x)
  \;=\;
  \begin{cases}
    2^{n}\dbinom{n}{r}, & r = s,\\[2pt]
    0, & r \ne s;
  \end{cases}
\]
that is, they are orthogonal with respect to the weights $\binom{n}{x}$ on $\{0, 1, \dots, n\}$.

